'''Xi'an''' was a [[Twi'lek]] [[Gender|female]] [[mercenary]] from [[Ryloth]]. At some point, she worked with the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]]. Xi'an later encountered Djarin once more when the two of them were [[Ranzar Malk's crew|hired]] by [[Ranzar Malk]] to [[Bothan-Five incident|rescue]] [[Qin]], Xi'an's twin brother, who was [[Prison|imprisoned]] aboard the ''[[Bothan-5]]'', a [[New Republic Correctional Transport]]. The team intended to betray Djarin and leave him for [[Death|dead]], but Djarin managed to escape, and trapped the members of the team inside one of the [[transport]]'s cells.

==Biography==
===Early career===
{{Quote|Ask him about the job on Alzoc III.''"<br />"''I did what I had to.''"<br />"''Oh, but you liked it.|Xi'an and Din Djarin reminisce|<ref name="Chapter 6" />}}
Xi'an became a [[mercenary]], and at some point, worked with her twin brother [[Qin]],<ref name="SWCEUAE" /> the mercenary [[Ranzar Malk]], and the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]]. [[Job on Alzoc III (Din Djarin)|One of her jobs]], alongside Djarin, was on [[Alzoc III]]. At one point, Xi'an had a relationship with Djarin, but actions by Djarin led to the fallout of the group.<ref name="Chapter 6" />

===Meeting the Mandalorian again===
{{Quote|Didn't take you for the type. Maybe that code of yours has made you soft.|Xi'an, to Din Djarin regarding him taking care of Grogu|<ref name="Chapter 6" />}}
[[File:TheMandalorianChapter6.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Xi'an with her new mercenary team.]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|6}}</ref> Malk formed a [[Ranzar Malk's crew|team]] of mercenaries including Xi'an, the [[human]] [[Migs Mayfeld]], the [[Devaronian]] [[Burg]], and the [[droid]] [[Q9-0]] "Zero" to rescue Qin. Malk also called in the Mandalorian in order to use his [[Starship|ship]], the ''[[Razor Crest]]'', which was pre-[[Imperial Era]] and was off the [[Galactic Empire]] and [[New Republic]] grids. Xi'an went to greet Djarin while he met the rest of the team and waved a [[dagger]] at him. The team began planning their [[Bothan-Five incident|infiltration]] of the ''[[Bothan-5]]'', a [[New Republic Correctional Transport]] that was holding Qin. Djarin was skeptical about getting in trouble with the New Republic but Xi'an told him that the [[prison]] ship was crewed by droids, knowing that the bounty hunter hated droids.<ref name="Chapter 6" />

After determining their plan, the mercenaries began traveling for the prison ship on the ''Razor Crest'', which Zero [[pilot]]ed. The rest of the team sat in the cargo hold, where Djarin quarreled with Burg. Burg and Mayfeld also talked about Mandalorians and when Mayfeld mentioned Xi'an's experience with them, she asked Djarin to tell the pair about Alzoc III. When Burg tried to remove Djarin's [[helmet]], the bounty hunter fought back and the Devaronian accidentally opened a door, revealing [[Din Grogu|Grogu]]. Mayfeld asked if Xi'an and Djarin made it and Xi'an asked if he had gone soft when he said it was a pet.<ref name="Chapter 6" />

===The job===
{{Quote|Brother!''"<br />"''Sister.|Xi'an and Qin reunite|<ref name="Chapter 6" />}}
Zero announced to the rest of the team that the ''Razor Crest'' was approaching the prison ship and began maneuvering it to land on the [[transport]] unnoticed. Xi'an was frustrated that the droid did not give them a countdown. After defeating a group of [[N5 sentry droid]]s, Xi'an and the rest of the team arrived in a control room where the human [[Lant Davan]] was working. He turned and pointed his [[blaster pistol]] at the group as Djarin expressed surprise at an organic worker being aboard the ship. He refused to [[Death|kill]] Davan, resulting in a standoff with the rest of the team. As Djarin and Mayfeld argued the topic, Xi'an murdered Davan by throwing a knife into his chest.<ref name="Chapter 6" />

[[File:Xian-Qin-reunited.png|thumb|right|275px|Xi'an is reunited with her brother.]]
Upon reaching Qin's cell, Burg pushed Djarin into the cell and locked the door. The Mandalorian eventually managed to escape, however, and locked the [[blast door]]s throughout the prison ship. He incapacitated Xi'an and the other members of the gang, locking them in a prison cell, and killed Zero. Djarin would return to Malk with Qin and receive the reward for the bounty, though Malk and Qin were attacked soon after by a trio of [[X-wing starfighter]]s who had traced a [[Homing beacon|tracking beacon]] that Djarin had left on Qin.<ref name="Chapter 6" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Xian-ChromeBlack2023.png|thumb|left|180px|Xi'an was both flamboyant and ruthless.]]
A [[Color|purple]]-skinned and blue-eyed [[Twi'lek]] [[Gender|female]] from [[Ryloth]],<ref name="SWCEUAE" /> Xi'an was skilled with bladed weapons. She had an eccentric personality and also claimed to be capable of moving beyond old grudges and working professionally alongside a personal enemy. Xi'an had no qualms with murdering Davan, and she also betrayed Djarin along with the rest of the team.<ref name="Chapter 6" />

==Skills and abilities==
Athletic and agile, Xi'an was proficient with melee weapons, such as knives, and could throw them with great accuracy.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|xi-an|Xi'an}}</ref>

==Equipment==
Xi'an carried several throwing knives and wore a maroon, long-sleeved shirt with brown pants and a belt.<ref name="Chapter 6" />

==Behind the scenes==
Xi'an first appeared in [[Chapter 6: The Prisoner|Chapter 6]] of the [[2019]] television show ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Chapter 6" /> which aired on [[December 13]], 2019,<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|work=[https://dtcimedia.disney.com Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]|archivedate=20230315011507}}</ref> and was portrayed by [[Natalia Tena]], with [[Katherine O'Donovan]] serving as a stunt double.<ref name="Chapter 6" /> The character was first revealed in a trailer leading up to the show's release on [[August 23]], 2019.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|aOC8E8z_ifw|The Mandalorian &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+ &#124; Streaming Nov. 12|sw_url=video/the-mandalorian-official-trailer}}</ref> Xi'an shares her name with the [[Wikipedia:Xi'an|Chinese city]] that notably contained the tomb of [[Wikipedia:Qin Shi Huang|Emperor Qin]].<ref name="Xi'an, Britannica">{{WebCite|url=https://www.britannica.com/place/Xian-China|text=Xi'an|archivedate=20201017183516}}</ref>

